  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rebuild flood damaged Savannah Research Centre</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Savannah Research Centre has contributed vastly towards biodiversity conservation in a global biodiversity hotspot. The centre is in Mbuluzi Game Reserve in Eswatini, Southern Africa &amp; has contributed over 170 publications since 2005. It provides important data &amp; skills for conservation action. Students from universities such as UNESWA, UF, UWITS, Wageningen, UEA, Auburn etc. make valuable contributions. The research centre has been massively hit by floods and we are striving to rebuild it.</narrative>
  </description>
